{"Meet fallback destructures evt.destinationCalendar ?? [] and immediately reads mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration, which throws when destinationCalendar is empty or null instead of safely falling back to Daily": 0.7920043468475342, "Calendar.createEvent interface now requires a second credentialId parameter, but this is a breaking API contract change that needs every caller/wrapper to be verified against the new signature": 0.7321678996086121, "Google update/delete fallback paths search destinationCalendar by comparing cal.externalId to the already-supplied externalCalendarId, so when that argument is absent they cannot recover the host destination calendar and fall back to primary, which can update/delete the wrong calendar or leave stale events for non-primary or multi-calendar bookings": 0.9850753545761108, "Cancellation bookingCalendarReference was changed from find(...) to filter(...), but the inner logic still assumes a single reference and only deletes events found in updatedBookings, leaving external calendar events undeleted for bookings with multiple _calendar references or multiple destination calendars": 0.26551875472068787, "Booking creation treats evt.destinationCalendar as an array but only connects evt.destinationCalendar[0] in Prisma, so collective events with multiple host calendars lose every destination calendar except the first at persistence time": 0.9156436324119568, "getConnectedDestinationCalendars calls getConnectedCalendars with user.destinationCalendar?.externalId, but the destination calendar relation is now modeled as an array, so the matching logic can only see one calendar and will miss additional host calendars": 0.03320050239562988, "Several booking-derived event builders reconstruct destinationCalendar by wrapping a single booking/user destination calendar in an array, dropping additional host destination calendars before reminder, confirm, reschedule, update, or sync flows reach EventManager": 0.9955518841743469, "getUserTopBanners.handler passes ctx.user.destinationCalendar?.externalId to getConnectedCalendars(), but destinationCalendar has been converted to an array elsewhere, so users with multiple destination calendars will not be matched correctly": 0.028050493448972702, "BrokenIntegrationEmail only inspects the first element of calEvent.destinationCalendar array, so for multi-host collective bookings the email can describe the wrong calendar/app if the first destination calendar is not the failing one": 0.8411751389503479, "Cancellation payload builds destinationCalendar as a single-item list from bookingToDelete.destinationCalendar or bookingToDelete.user.destinationCalendar, reducing collective bookings with multiple destination calendars to one calendar for email/webhook/cancel flows": 0.9870008230209351, "ICS generation Office365 suppression guard checks only destinationCalendar[0]?.integration, so with the new array shape the function may incorrectly emit an ICS file for events that should be suppressed when Office365 is not the first element": 0.4113195836544037}